    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0432" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4729: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-27T10:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                                1927—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>112. Espinosa, Argüello, and Cordero Reyes<anchor n="53" xml:id="d306-f1"/>
                    designated by Sacasa to confer with Stimson, left Puerto Cabezas this morning at
                    6 o’clock on the destroyer <hi rendition="#italic">Preston</hi>. They should
                    arrive at Managua, Saturday or Sunday.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d306-f2"/> Stimson
                    would be glad to be fully informed as to authority discussed in his telegram
                        109<anchor n="55" xml:id="d306-f3"/> before their arrival.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d306-f1" n="53" xml:id="d306-f1-content">
                <p>Dr. Leonardo Argüello, Minister of Gobernación, and Dr. Manuel Cordero Reyes,
                    private secretary to Dr. Sacasa.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d306-f2" n="54" xml:id="d306-f2-content">
                <p>i. e., April 30 or May 1.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d306-f3" n="55" xml:id="d306-f3-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg328">p. 328</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
